# DO Manager Hooks and Utilities Conventions

## Context
- This rule applies to all hook and utility files in the project
- Hooks have specific patterns and naming conventions
- Utility functions follow specific organization and export patterns

## Requirements
- Maintain consistent naming conventions for hooks and utility functions
- Follow established patterns for hook implementation
- Organize utility functions by domain
- Use proper TypeScript types for all functions

## Hooks Structure
- All hooks must be in the `src/hooks` directory
- Use `use` prefix for all hook names
- Hooks should always be function declarations (not arrow functions)
- Always include return type annotations for hooks
- Implement proper cleanup in hooks with side effects

## Utility Functions
- Place utility functions in appropriate domain folders under `src/utils`
- Export utility functions as named exports
- Group related utility functions in the same file
- Include TypeScript type definitions for all parameters and return values
- Implement proper error handling

## Examples
<example>
// Good hook example
import { useState, useEffect } from 'react';
import { SomeType } from '@/types/some-type';

export function useCustomHook(param: string): { data: SomeType | null; isLoading: boolean } {
  const [data, setData] = useState<SomeType | null>(null);
  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(true);
  
  useEffect(() => {
    // Effect logic
    return () => {
      // Cleanup logic
    };
  }, [param]);
  
  return { data, isLoading };
}
</example>

<example type="invalid">
// Bad hook example
import React from 'react';

// Missing 'use' prefix and proper types
export const customHook = (param) => {
  const [data, setData] = React.useState();
  
  React.useEffect(() => {
    // Effect with no cleanup
  });
  
  return data;
}
</example>

## Critical Rules
- ALWAYS use 'use' prefix for hook names
- ALWAYS include TypeScript types for parameters and return values
- ALWAYS implement proper cleanup in useEffect hooks
- ALWAYS handle loading and error states in data fetching hooks
- NEVER use default exports for hooks or utilities
- PLACE all hooks in src/hooks directory
- ORGANIZE utility functions by domain
- USE function declarations for hooks 